    "The universally quantified input t is any finite nonempty ordered full binary tree with pairs of reals at its leaves. There is no prescribed leaf count, balancing assumption, or restriction on signs, magnitudes, or cancellation. All arithmetic values, perturbations, and model outputs are real.",
